{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Duplicate determination — runtime-confirmed, linked duplicates->lemuroid-compliant-hoopoe (39a2-4832-e436-4850).\n\nRUNTIME REPRODUCTION (deterministic local remote): a fresh clone with the default broad refspec (+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*) and an unrelated large 'tickets' branch. With the target commit already present locally (full 40-hex SHA c2b79f4b...), resolve_ref(sha, clone, fetch=True, blobless=False) still issued exactly:\n  git -C <clone> -c http.lowSpeedLimit=1000 -c http.lowSpeedTime=10 fetch --quiet --no-filter origin\ni.e. a broad no-filter fetch whose scope expands through remote.origin.fetch to every head — no target ref passed — even though rev_parse resolves the SHA with zero network. This is the recorded mechanism (repo_snapshot.resolve_ref ~L262-266 -> git_fetch.fetch_origin ~L256-283) confirmed empirically.\n\nWHY DUPLICATE (not merely related): lemuroid-compliant-hoopoe has the same title/root cause (attested ref materialization broad-fetches all origin heads), declared file_impact on the IDENTICAL seam (src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py, src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py, tests/unit/test_snapshot_targeted_fetch.py), and its ACs subsume this ticket's. hoopoe's own Context section cites the SAME 512.139s run (from unromantic-ferny-arawana) that this ticket's Proof section cites. The fixes would edit the same function bodies with the same intent; a second competing Gerrit change would be redundant.\n\nSHARED CODE PATH FOR THE REVIEWER: the correct fix lives in resolve_ref — skip the general fetch_origin() when ref is a full 40-hex SHA that rev_parse resolves locally (return it directly); keep the general fetch for moving branches/tags; keep the existing targeted-fetch fallback for an absent SHA. Blob acquisition is UNAFFECTED because it is handled separately by _ensure_blobs_present() (targeted 'git fetch --no-filter --refetch <sha>'), so a present-SHA short-circuit still materializes all blobs.\n\nDISPOSITION: not opening a competing change. hoopoe owns the code fix; this ticket is left claimed for coordinator/human disposition (recommend closing as duplicate once hoopoe's change lands and satisfies the shared acceptance criteria). If hoopoe stalls, this ticket can be reopened for independent implementation using the minimal fix above."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787552186900107001,"uuid":"eb1ee7d3-2074-4de6-bb49-ba7381133413"}